.TH BERIGNA 1 "November 2026" "berigna 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
berigna \- sign and verify documents with the Peruvian DNIe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B berigna
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B berigna
signs and verifies documents with the certificates of the Peruvian
electronic identity card (DNIe), read from a smart card reader.
It signs PDF documents in PAdES and other files in CAdES and XAdES,
from the basic signature (B\-B) to the long\-term archival signature
(B\-LTA), with a timestamp from an IOFE accredited authority.
.
It verifies signed documents with the ETSI indications, signs batches
of documents with a single PIN, draws a visible signature with text,
a rubrica, a logo or a QR code, and writes verification reports in
JSON and PDF. The interface is in Peruvian Spanish and Southern
Quechua.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I file
Open the file: berigna signs it or verifies it, depending on whether
it already carries a signature. Several files at once open the batch
mode. Files can also be dragged onto the window.
.SH SINGLE INSTANCE
Opening a file while berigna is already running delivers it to the
running instance instead of starting a new one (RF\-073).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/berigna/
cache of the INDECOPI trusted list and the history database.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/berigna/
technical log and pending failure reports.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pyhanko (1)
